# Rookery Stacks - the eighth island of the library's plan The City That Never Sank (SL13, Highwater, chapter 8)
# The poor quarter, on the city's lowest roofs: shanty huts on two drowned towers' roofs (hut on roof - two high), more
# on the key, rope bridges, washing everywhere, a soup kitchen under a wooden roof, empty water barrels, a tollgate of
# spikes on the causeway, rats in the barrels, screechers on the roofs, a llama pen, a trader. Quest "The Lowest Roofs"
# (24 steps, STORY 10-24: the bots and the ration tins first, Maud and Pip Penn, Ines's torn ledger page on the great chimney, Crane's ration order in the bathhouse cellar; the boiler valve machine gone): the soup kitchen, the Rookery's petition, four rats, the titanium tools' plans (the smithy), the tollgate,
# three screechers, the advanced backpack's plans, three water tokens, the elders' plan, the electric zipline tool's
# plans, the storm warning.
#
# Points: the key 0 0 (r about 38, levelled at 2 round 0 0); the soup kitchen at -6 -8; the trader at -6 8; the smithy
# hut at 6 -10; the llama pen round 16 10; the causeway along x -12 from z -18 to -25 (the tollgate at -12 -21); the two
# towers' roofs x -15..-9 and -3..3, z -34.5..-25.5 (deck 1), a bridge between them at z -30, a hut on each; the
# treasure within 10 of 12 -8.
include lib_sea
include lib_rt
include lib_huts
include lib_features
include lib_highwater
include lib_areas
# RESIZE 10-24: Radius 38 -> 80 (Height 4 -> 4), the old content moved -6.6 -22.1 as one frame (push) so its sea side stays at the coast; the island grows behind it.
# DEEP 10-24: Chimney Tor: the poor quarter's great chimney, a drowned bathhouse cellar, butler bots that guard the stack doors - and hot water for the Rookery.
new
