story rk_top|Torn ledger page|Note_Paper|The page Ines Marlowe tore from the Cistern ledger - Crane's ballast account.
story rk_deep|Ration order|Note_Paper|Crane's order holding back the Rookery's rations until it moves away.
story ration|Ration tin|Bolt|A sealed Authority ration tin. In the Rookery one tin opens any store.
note rk_hint Maud Penn's note | Nailed to the cold boiler, in a careful old hand -\n\nStranger. The bots came the week after Lowstreet, with the Authority's ration tins, and they guard the tins better than they ever guarded us. Thank you for stopping them. One of them used to bring my tea.\n\nI am Maud Penn. I keep these roofs, as much as anyone keeps anything here. Two thousand of us came up from Lowstreet with what we could carry. My son Jonah drove the tram. He did not come up.\n\nThe diver - Ines - left something on top of the great chimney, the night before she went back down. She said: give it to whoever comes with my chalk. Take a tin; the box is padlocked with one. Old habits.\n\nAnd if you see my granddaughter Pip, tell her I am not cross about the tram. Much.\n\n- Maud
prop rk_topchest on.open=message||A ledger page, folded small, in oilcloth - the page torn from the Cistern ledger. BALLAST ACCOUNT. Piles 1 to 4: cracked. Weight required at the foot, by the spring tides: two million tons. Southern district basin: to be filled. Rookery: to be lightened. Iron and stone: all available. Initialled at the foot, very neat: A.C.
prop rk_deepchest on.open=message||A ration order, sealed in wax: ROOKERY RATIONS TO BE HELD AT THE BATHHOUSE UNTIL THE ROOKERY REMOVES ITSELF. The roofs are overloaded. Every family on them is weight the Crown does not need. - Councillor A. Crane
note rk_topchest Great chimney deck box | A box lashed to the deck rail at the top of the great chimney.
loot rk_topchest story:rk_top*1;Scrap*2;Rope*1
note rk_deepchest Bathhouse cellar strongbox | A strongbox in the back room of the bathhouse cellar.
loot rk_deepchest story:rk_deep*1;MetalIngot*1;Plastic*2
note rk_ledge Climber's cache | A climber's cache on a ledge off the trail - rope, a flask, a few bolts.
loot rk_ledge Rope*2;Bolt*2;Scrap*2
prop rk_ledge loot.refill=0
loot rk_boatcrate Plastic*3;Scrap*2;MetalIngot*1
note rk_tin1 Ration tin | A sealed ration tin, stamped AUTHORITY KITCHENS.
note rk_tin2 Ration tin | A sealed ration tin, stamped AUTHORITY KITCHENS.
note rk_tin3 Ration tin | A sealed ration tin, stamped AUTHORITY KITCHENS.
