loot rk_tin2 story:ration*1;Watermelon*1
loot rk_tin3 story:ration*1;Watermelon*1
note rk_hoard Glass hoard | The Rookery's glass hoard: bottles washed and kept for when the water comes.
loot rk_hoard Glass*4;TradeToken*2
prop rk_ledge if.open=has|Tangaroa_KeyCard|1
prop rk_ledge else.open=message||A card lock on the box - a Tangaroa keycard would open it.

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Rookery Stacks
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Highwater's poor quarter on the city's lowest roofs: huts stacked on drowned towers, washing on every line, a soup kitchen, a tollgate of spikes - and empty water barrels. The eighth island of The City That Never Sank.
island on.arrive=message||Huts on huts, washing on every line. A long queue at a soup kitchen. Every water barrel you can see is empty.

story watertoken|Water token|Bolt|A Rookery water token - one barrel's worth, stamped by the elders.

prop rook tint.color=#857c70
prop rook tint.amount=0.35
prop skyline tint.color=#7a8088
prop skyline tint.amount=0.4
prop rats creature.count=4
prop rats creature.respawn=0
prop screechers creature.count=3
prop screechers creature.respawn=0
prop llamas creature.count=2
prop storm obj.name=storm
prop storm beh.hidden=1
prop elders on.read=show|storm

note petition Rookery petition | PETITION OF THE ROOKERY\n\nTo the Authority, the Fleet and the Union:\n\nOur barrels are empty. Our children drink rain. The water you sell would fill them all.\n\nWe ask for nothing but our share.\n\n(Four hundred marks below it. Nobody answered.)\n\n(Under the marks, in a careful old hand: We sent it to all three. The Fleet sent a boat of filters, the Union sent a diver, and the Council sent a form asking how much the Rookery weighs. I wrote: about as much as it ever did, Councillor, minus the children's dinners. - Maud Penn, for the elders)
note pipnote Pip's note | Weighed down with a gull egg (empty, I checked) -\n\nTO THE PERSON WITH THE CHALK HOOK. Nan says you are coming. Nan is never wrong except about bedtimes.\n\nI am Pip Penn and I am nine. I count the barrels every morning. Empty, empty, empty. Then I come up here and count the trams. There are no trams. There is one, under the water, and my dad drove it.\n\nI swapped my tin tram to the pedlar Rook for a whole flask of clean water, for Nan's cough. It was the right thing. It was also the worst thing. If you see Rook, he has a little blue tram with a dent. That one is mine.\n\nWhen we go to the shoal I am going to build a tram line out of driftwood.\n\n- Pip
note tollsign Tollgate | ROOKERY TOLLGATE\nNo Authority. No Fleet. No Union.\nEveryone else - welcome.
note elders Rookery elders' plan | THE ELDERS' PLAN\n\nIf the city will not share, we leave it. There is a shoal outside the city, our own - sand, a spring, room for huts.\n\nWe need someone to clear the way. Someone who is not Authority, Fleet or Union.\n\n(Maud's hand: I would rather stay and be heard than go and be forgotten. But I am old, and Pip is not. - M.P.)
note storm Storm warning | Scrawled in a hurry on the back of the plan -\n\nTHE GLASS IS FALLING. A storm is coming over the Crown. The councils will meet on the four roofs tonight to settle the city's water.\n\nGo. Whatever they decide, the Rookery will be drowned by it unless someone speaks for us.\n\nTake the page. Read it to them. And look at the Councillor's face when you say the word ballast. - M.P.
note smithy Rookery smithy | The smithy's chest: the titanium tools' plans, wrapped in a rag.
note packhut Packer's hut | A packer's chest: the advanced backpack's plans.
note eldershut Elders' hut | The elders' chest: the electric zipline tool's plans.
note barrel1 Water barrel | An empty water barrel - only a token at the bottom.
note barrel2 Water barrel | An empty water barrel - only a token at the bottom.
note barrel3 Water barrel | An empty water barrel - only a token at the bottom.
loot smithy Blueprint_TitaniumTools*1;MetalIngot*2
prop smithy loot.refill=0
loot packhut Blueprint_BackpackAdvanced*1;Leather*3;Rope*2
prop packhut loot.refill=0
loot eldershut Blueprint_ZiplineToolElectric*1;Battery*1;Rope*2
prop eldershut loot.refill=0
loot barrel1 story:watertoken*1
prop barrel1 loot.refill=0
loot barrel2 story:watertoken*1
prop barrel2 loot.refill=0
loot barrel3 story:watertoken*1
prop barrel3 loot.refill=0

